t').change(function(){location.href='/results/' + $('#other_games_select').val();})"]] " | " [:a {:href "/event_names/319"} "Event type"]] [:h1 {:class "event_title"} "Horizontal Bar, Men" [:small {}]] [:table {:class "biodata"} [:tbody {} [:tr {} [:th {} "Date"] [:td {} "14 – 23 August 2004"]] [:tr {} [:th {} "Status"] [:td {} "Olympic"]] [:tr {} [:th {} "Location"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/venues/782"} "Olympiako Kleisto Gymnastirio, Olympiako Athletiko Kentro Athinon Spiros Loues, Maroussi"]]] [:tr {} [:th {} "Participants"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/events/70872"} "79 from 29 countries"]]]]] [:div {:class "description"} [:p {} "The format was the same as it had been from 1984-2000, with eight gymnasts advancing from the team all-around, but no more than two per nation. Russia’s " [:a {:href "/athletes/30978"} "Aleksey Nemov"] " was the defending champion and made the final. He performed what appeared to be a difficult routine with flawless execution except for a small step on landing, but was given a score of 9.725, causing the crowd to erupt in a noisy protest. After a consultation the judges adjusted the score to 9.762, which did little to placate the crowd. American " [:a {:href "/athletes/91591"} "Paul Hamm"] " was up next and similarly performed well except for a small step on landing, earning a score of 9.812, which only further angered the crowd. Italian " [:a {:href "/athletes/91501"} "Igor Cassina"] ", who had been the 2003 World bronze medalist, then did his routine, matching Hamm’s score, but winning the gold medal on a tie-breaker. Japan’s " [:a {:href "/athletes/107227"} "Isao Yoneda"] " and Hamm’s twin brother, " [:a {:href "/athletes/91590"} "Morgan"] ", tied for third with 9.787, with Yoneda winning the bronze medal, also by tie-breaker. Because of ties in qualifying, this event unusually had 10 finalists."] "\n"] [:table {:class "table table-striped"} [:thead {} [:tr {} [:th {} "Pos"] [:th {} "Number"] [:th {} "Competitor"] [:th {} "NOC"] [:th {} "Points